{
  "id": "remove-duplicates-from-sorted-list-ii",
  "questionId": "remove-duplicates-from-sorted-list-ii",
  "slug": "remove-duplicates-from-sorted-list-ii",
  "title": "Remove Duplicates from Sorted List II",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Linked list",
  "patterns": [
    "linked list",
    "two pointers"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "since the list is sorted, every duplicate of a value sits in one contiguous run - you never need to look far away to find all copies of a value",
    "the tricky part is the list's head itself might be part of a duplicate run and need deleting - a dummy node placed before the head sidesteps that special case",
    "keep a pointer to the last node you're sure belongs in the result, starting at the dummy node",
    "look ahead from that pointer: if the next node's value repeats (matches the one after it), advance through the entire run of matching values and skip all of them, relinking past the whole run; otherwise just advance normally by one node",
    "continue until you run out of nodes, then return the values starting after the dummy"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "removing only one extra copy of a duplicated value instead of every copy (the problem wants zero copies of any duplicated value, not one)",
    "not using a dummy/sentinel node before the head, causing bugs when the head itself is part of a duplicate run that must be deleted",
    "comparing a node only to its immediate previous neighbor instead of checking the whole contiguous run of equal values before deciding to skip it",
    "off-by-one errors when relinking the pointer past a deleted run, leaving a dangling or incorrect connection"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A sorted singly linked list is given to you as an array `nums`, where\n`nums[i]` is the value of the i-th node in order.\n\n**Delete every node whose value occurs more than once in the list, and return the values remaining, in order.**\n\nThis leaves only the nodes whose values are unique in the original list, not just one copy of each duplicated value, but zero copies.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "0 <= nums.length <= 300",
      "-100 <= nums[i] <= 100",
      "nums is sorted in non-decreasing order"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "the empty list",
      "every value in the list is a duplicate, leaving an empty result",
      "the duplicated run is at the very start or the very end of the list",
      "a value appears three or more times, not just twice"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [1, 2, 3, 3, 4, 4, 5]",
        "output": "[1, 2, 5]",
        "expectedOutput": "[1, 2, 5]",
        "explanation": "3 and 4 each occur more than once, so every copy of them is removed, leaving 1, 2, and 5"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [1, 1, 1, 2, 3]",
        "output": "[2, 3]",
        "expectedOutput": "[2, 3]",
        "explanation": "1 occurs three times, so all three copies are removed"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [1, 2, 3]",
        "output": "[1, 2, 3]",
        "expectedOutput": "[1, 2, 3]",
        "explanation": "no value repeats, so nothing is removed"
      }
